          3 NOTE       9 Not tested                                                 The policy was rebuilt by this file, and the permission ids it now carries include the test fixtures'                                                                                                    auth.uspRebuildTenantAccessPolicy resolves Data.Read, Data.Insert and Data.Update across EVERY application, so after this run the predicates name the ROWSEC and AUTHZTEST permission ids alongside any real ones. That is correct -- the codes are the contract, not the ids -- but it means the deployed policy in a development database reflects whatever the tests last created. Re-run 120_rls_policy.sql to rebuild from the real catalogue, and remember that 100_auth_functions.sql, 065_auth_effective_permission.sql and 030_auth_tenant.sql cannot be re-run at all while the policy is bound (error 3729): drop it first with EXEC auth.uspRebuildTenantAccessPolicy @Action = N'Drop'.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            
          3 NOTE       9 Not tested                                                 Nothing here was read through a stored procedure, so ownership chaining past the policy is unexamined                                                                                                    Every statement in section 6 touched the tables directly. A security policy evaluates its predicates in the POLICY's context, so a caller needs no permission on auth.ProfilePermissionScope or auth.TenantClosure to be filtered by them -- measured while building 120_rls_policy.sql -- but whether a procedure that reads dbo.CaseFile on an application user's behalf behaves identically is a Phase 6 question, when there are procedures to ask it of.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   
